---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { layers, href } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Architecture"
  section="Architecture"
  description="Explore the proposed ContinuumOS architecture: an original Rust kernel, explicit boundaries, typed actions and controlled state transfer."
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap">
    <span class="section-label">THE ENGINEERING / EXPLICIT BY DESIGN</span>
    <h1>
      A continuous experience.
      <br />
      <span class="mint">Deliberate boundaries.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Continuity needs more than a smooth transition. It needs an architecture that knows what owns
      state, who has authority and when old code can stop.
    </p>
    <span class="pill partial">
      KERNEL + HOSTED SUBSET ACCEPTED LOCALLY · GUEST ARCHITECTURE GATES PENDING
    </span>
  </section>
  <div class="page-content wrap">
    <section class="architecture-grid" aria-label="Interactive architecture explorer">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">SELECT A LAYER</span>
        <div class="layer-map">
          {layers.map((layer, i) => (
            <button
              class="layer-button"
              data-layer={layer.id}
              aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
              aria-controls="layer-detail"
            >
              <span class="layer-icon">0{i + 1}</span>
              <span>
                <span class="layer-name">{layer.name}</span>
                <small>{layer.tag}</small>
              </span>
              <span class="layer-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                ↗
              </span>
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="layer-detail" class="layer-details" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
        <span class="micro" id="layer-tag">
          {layers[0].tag}
        </span>
        <h2 id="layer-title">{layers[0].name}</h2>
        <p id="layer-text">{layers[0].text}</p>
        <div class="boundary">
          <span class="micro">THE BOUNDARY</span>
          <p id="layer-boundary">{layers[0].boundary}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <details class="static-layers">
      <summary>Read all architecture layers as text</summary>
      {layers.map((layer) => (
        <article>
          <h3>{layer.name}</h3>
          <p>{layer.text}</p>
          <p class="micro">{layer.boundary}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </details>
    <section class="article-block section-space">
      <span class="section-label">TWO DISTINCT PROBLEMS</span>
      <h2>
        Keep working.
        <br />
        Be able to start again.
      </h2>
      <div class="comparison">
        <div>
          <span class="index">LIVE STATE TRANSFER</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:16px">During the session</h3>
          <p>
            A compatible replacement carries accepted document state into a new application
            generation. Authority, in-flight requests and old execution need a controlled handover.
            A universal kernel hot reload is not assumed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="index copper">BOOT RECOVERY</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:16px">Across a restart</h3>
          <p>
            A known-good generation and rescue path help the machine boot after a failed change.
            That is a separate test from keeping unsaved work alive during an update. A booting
            image proves neither on its own.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="two-column article-block">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">ONE SET OF ACTIONS</span>
        <h2>Intent has a contract.</h2>
        <p>
          A button, shortcut or authorized automation should invoke the same versioned operation.
          Inputs, context revisions and permissions are validated by the provider. No caller gets
          special authority for being an assistant.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI is an optional, isolated experiment after the first state-preserving guest reload. The
          core desktop must stand on its own.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="code-caption">ILLUSTRATIVE WEBSITE DEMO ACTION · NOT AN OS WIRE SCHEMA</span>
        <pre
          class="code-block"
          tabindex="0"
          role="region"
          aria-label="Illustrative website demo action"
        ><code>{`{
  action: "appearance.apply",
  arguments: { theme: "dusk" },
  result: "appearance changed; document retained"
}`}</code></pre>
        <a class="text-link" href={href('concepts/')} style="margin-top:22px">
          Explore the shared demo actions <span>↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="note">
      <h3>Evidence determines the implementation.</h3>
      <p>
        Process isolation, service replacement and guest UI integration are proposed and unproven.
        Custom Rust is provisionally selected after the hosted Slint/custom comparison; guest
        confirmation remains pending. Hosted resource publication preserves state in the same
        process and window. Replacing an application process is a separate future gate.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script>
    import { layers } from '../data/site';
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-layer]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const layer = layers.find((item) => item.id === button.dataset.layer);
        if (!layer) return;
        document
          .querySelectorAll('[data-layer]')
          .forEach((item) => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === button)));
        const detail = document.getElementById('layer-detail');
        detail?.getAnimations().forEach((animation) => animation.cancel());
        if (detail?.animate && !matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)
          detail.animate(
            [
              { opacity: 0.45, translate: '0 6px' },
              { opacity: 1, translate: '0 0' },
            ],
            { duration: 280, easing: 'cubic-bezier(.2,.75,.2,1)' },
          );
        for (const [id, value] of Object.entries({
          'layer-tag': layer.tag,
          'layer-title': layer.name,
          'layer-text': layer.text,
          'layer-boundary': layer.boundary,
        })) {
          const element = document.getElementById(id);
          if (element) element.textContent = value;
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
